In article <224@uucs1.UUCP> rfp@uucs1.UUCP (Roger Powell) writes:
>
>9) How about a notepad - not part of inventory, just a little something
>to scribble on that is saved with the saved game, to jot notes to yourself
>on where you have left things, what intrinisics you have, etc.  I have
>seen suggestions where this would an inventory item - I contend it is for
>player convenience.  Otherwise, I would keep a handwritten sheet if the
>notepad cost me carrying weight or could be lost.

An easy way to do this might be to provide a command to invoke the users
favorite editor (via the EDITOR environment variable) and load in a file
that is named the same as the save file for the current game.  These "notes"
files could be stored in a directory (called "notes"?) parallel to the "save"
and "bones" directories.

This would be a great feature.  As it is now I keep a pad and pencil
beside me while playing so that I can jot down interesting tid bits of
information.                                                  Marc
